 "rule": "Band rule (Daniel, 2026-09-30, advantage-pr strategy §2): the books of a CEFR band share the band's objectives; no book is pinned to a GSE range. A1 band: Quest 4, 5, 6.1, 6.2 (GSE 22–29). A2 band: Adventure 7.1–9.3 (GSE 30–42). First teaching: books[b].objectives are the objectives that book b brings into the band. Each is a target in 1 or more of its lessons. Quest 4 counts as written. Each band's objectives that no book teaches yet are sorted by GSE and split evenly over its books, so the books move up the GSE scale. Recycling (Daniel, 2026-10-06): each package lists every objective that it gives practice in (tags.targetObjectives and tags.supportingObjectives). The coverage report counts, for each objective, the packages after its first teaching that give practice in it. Each lesson map takes its other targets from the objectives with the lowest counts. levels[n]: the in-scope objectives of level n's own GSE range. The bank articles of level n and the level rule (3 or more packages of the level) use it.",
